PiST — third-party components and their licences
================================================

PiST itself is free software under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or
later. See LICENSE.

PiST *drives* the components below as separate programs, passing command-line
arguments. It does not link against them, does not modify them, and does not
write their configuration files. That separation is deliberate and is what keeps
the licensing straightforward (see docs/PLAN.md §7).


Runtime dependencies (invoked as subprocesses, not distributed here)
---------------------------------------------------------------------

vasmm68k_mot — the assembler
    Copyright (c) 2002-2026 Volker Barthelmann.
    NOT free software. Its terms permit redistribution *without modification*
    and use for non-commercial purposes; commercial use requires the author's
    written consent except for the M68k/AmigaOS case. PiST therefore never
    patches it and never commits it to this repository.
    Source and licence: http://sun.hasenbraten.de/vasm/

hatari — the emulator
    GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. Hatari's own readme states
    that linking it statically or dynamically makes a combined work, which is one
    reason PiST runs it as a separate process.
    https://www.hatari-emu.org/

A TOS ROM image is also required. Original Atari TOS images remain copyrighted
and are never distributed with PiST; the user supplies one. The ROM's version is
read from the image header, and TOS 1.04 or later is required for the
GEMDOS-hard-disk run path. EmuTOS (GPLv2) is a free alternative.
    https://emutos.sourceforge.net/


